# ============================================================================
# 60-electron-inspector.patch - the electron://fingerprint/ Inspector.
#
# Part of the fp-fingerprint patch set. Apply in filename order:
#   00-core.patch -> 10-blink-core.patch -> 20-blink-modules.patch ->
#   30-webrtc.patch -> 40-net-tls.patch -> 50-electron-glue.patch ->
#   60-electron-inspector.patch
#
# WHAT THIS ADDS
#   A privileged WebUI at electron://fingerprint/ that reports the ACTIVE
#   fingerprint configuration of the BrowserContext it is opened on: per-group
#   coverage across all 63 fp_* keys, and cross-layer consistency findings.
#
# WHY A NEW SCHEME
#   The Inspector is Electron-implemented and must not be reachable at
#   chrome://fingerprint (which would imply a Chromium upstream WebUI). It is
#   served on its own scheme, registered in three places that are INDEPENDENT
#   and all three are required - missing any one produces a different,
#   misleading failure:
#
#     1. url::AddStandardScheme (browser + renderer). Without it the URL does
#        not parse and every navigation fails ERR_INVALID_URL (-300).
#     2. ContentBrowserClient::GetAdditionalWebUISchemes. Without it content
#        does not treat the scheme as WebUI and navigation fails
#        ERR_FAILED (-2).
#     3. URLDataSource::ShouldServiceRequest. The default implementation
#        (content/public/browser/url_data_source.h) allows ONLY chrome: and
#        devtools:, so on any new scheme the data source is found and then
#        refused - ERR_INVALID_URL again, with StartDataRequest never called.
#
#   Registration must also happen before url::LockSchemeRegistries() and before
#   any GURL is constructed: PreMainMessageLoopRun is too late and trips
#   "Trying to add a scheme after the lists have been used"
#   (url/url_util.cc:503). PreCreateMainMessageLoop is early enough.
#
# WHY THE PAGE IS SELF-CONTAINED
#   Normally a WebUI serves its HTML, fetches JSON, and loads <script src>.
#   NONE of those subresource paths work in this build - and this is not
#   specific to the new scheme. Verified on stock chrome://accessibility:
#     - fetch('chrome://resources/js/cr.js')          -> "Failed to fetch"
#     - addWebUiListener                              -> undefined
#   So the data source inlines the script AND the data into the index response,
#   which travels the one path that does work: the main document load.
#
# TWO CONFIG STORES - BOTH MUST BE READ
#   SessionPreferences      <- session.setFingerprintConfig({...})
#   WebContentsPreferences  <- new BrowserView({ webPreferences: { fingerprint } })
#
#   The Client uses the SECOND one (Client/main.js builds a per-tab BrowserView
#   with "fingerprint" in webPreferences). Reading only SessionPreferences shows
#   an empty profile for a real Client tab - the primary case the Inspector
#   exists to inspect - and reads as "verified clean" when nothing was read.
#   Both are merged, with the per-tab config winning on conflict, and the merge
#   happens BEFORE the coverage counters are computed.
#
# NOTE ON COVERAGE GROUPS
#   The group/key table in fingerprint_ui.cc mirrors Client/fp-schema.js. That
#   duplication is deliberate (C++ cannot read the JS schema) but the two MUST
#   stay in sync; test-inspector.js asserts the total is 63.
#
# NEW FILES (not diffable, listed here because they are part of the change):
#   shell/browser/ui/webui/fingerprint_ui.h        - WebUIController + URLDataSource
#   shell/browser/ui/webui/fingerprint_ui.cc       - data source, page assembly,
#                                                    live-data builder
#   shell/browser/ui/webui/fingerprint_ui_page.h   - raw-string HTML + JS
# ============================================================================
#
# --- filenames.gni
#   Register the three new WebUI sources in the build.
#
# --- shell/browser/electron_browser_client.cc
#   Declare "electron" as a WebUI scheme (see registration step 2 above).
#
# --- shell/browser/electron_browser_main_parts.cc
#   url::AddStandardScheme + AddCorsEnabledScheme for "electron", in
#   PreCreateMainMessageLoop - early enough to beat the GURL-usage DCHECK.
#
# --- shell/browser/electron_web_ui_controller_factory.cc
#   Route host "fingerprint" to FingerprintUI.
#
# --- shell/common/electron_constants.h
#   Define kElectronUIScheme = "electron".
#
# --- shell/renderer/renderer_client_base.cc
#   Mirror the browser-process scheme registration in the renderer; schemes are
#   per-process and a mismatch makes the URL unparseable on one side.
diff --git a/filenames.gni b/filenames.gni
